🔍 Server Error Diagnosis

There are two separate issues killing your server:

Issue 1: API Server won't build (the immediate error)

The api-server's build script runs node ./build.mjs, but pnpm resolves node to /Users/AjieethA/.local/bin/node (a Hermes symlink) which the sandbox blocks. When you run it normally in Terminal, this should work fine — the sandbox is what causes that specific failure.

Issue 2: API Server crashes on startup (the real runtime error)

The lib/db/src/index.ts throws immediately if SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL is not set:

ts
if (!process.env.SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL) {
  throw new Error("SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL must be set ...");
}

Your .env currently has:

SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL=   ← EMPTY
SARVAM_VOICE_AGENTS_API_KEY=   ← EMPTY

So the API server crashes on startup before it can serve any requests, which means:

Voice calls fail → {"error":"Unable to start the Sarvam voice session"}
All /api/* routes return network errors
Issue 3: Sarvam API key missing

Even if the DB were connected, Sarvam would still fail because SARVAM_VOICE_AGENTS_API_KEY is empty → the route returns 503: "Sarvam Voice Agents is not configured".

